## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of stability and permutation-based sorting, ensuring candidates can separate data from its keys and reason about time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Stable sort
- Permutations
- Time/space complexity
- Merge-based sorting on indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function stableSortIndicesByValue(A){
  const idx = Array.from({length: A.length}, (_, i) => i);
  function merge(left, right){
    const res = [];
    let i = 0, j = 0;
    while (i < left.length && j < right.length){
      if (A[left[i]] <= A[right[j]]) res.push(left[i++]);
      else res.push(right[j++]);
    }
    while (i < left.length) res.push(left[i++]);
    while (j < right.length) res.push(right[j++]);
    return res;
  }
  function sort(arr){
    if (arr.length <= 1) return arr;
    const m = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);
    const L = sort(arr.slice(0, m));
    const R = sort(arr.slice(m));
    return merge(L, R);
  }
  const P = sort(idx);
  return { P, sorted: P.map(i => A[i]) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of multiple shortest paths and second-best paths with counting, using a single Dijkstra variant. It blends graph traversal and path combinatorics under constraints typical at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Two-best paths per node; counting paths for each distance tier
- Dijkstra relaxation with tie-handling
- Modulo counting for combinatorial paths

## Code Example
```javascript
// Two-best Dijkstra (conceptual)
function secondShortest(graph, s, t, MOD){
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const n = graph.length;
  const dist1 = Array(n).fill(INF);
  const dist2 = Array(n).fill(INF);
  const cnt1 = Array(n).fill(0);
  const cnt2 = Array(n).fill(0);
  dist1[s] = 0; cnt1[s] = 1;
  const pq = new MinHeap();
  pq.push([0, s]);
  while(!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [d, u] = pq.pop();
    if (d > dist2[u]) continue;
    for (const [v, w] of graph[u]){
      const nd = d + w;
      if (nd < dist1[v]){
        dist2[v] = dist1[v]; cnt2[v] = cnt1[v];
        dist1[v] = nd; cnt1[v] = cnt1[u];
        pq.push([nd, v]);
      } else if (nd === dist1[v]){
        cnt1[v] = (cnt1[v] + cnt1[u]) % MOD;
      } else if (nd > dist1[v] && nd < dist2[v]){
        dist2[v] = nd; cnt2[v] = cnt1[u];
        pq.push([nd, v]);
      } else if (nd === dist2[v]){
        cnt2[v] = (cnt2[v] + cnt1[u]) % MOD;
      }
    }
  }
  return [dist2[t], cnt2[t] % MOD];
}
```

